.TH BIGFLOATNORMALIZE 3 "2026-09-25" "BigNums 3" "Library Functions Manual"
.nr HY 0
.ds AD l
.SH NAME
bigFloatNormalize, bigFloatSetPrecision, bigFloatTruncate \- normalize or configure float precision
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <bignums.h>

int bigFloatNormalize(BigFloat *x);
int bigFloatSetPrecision(BigFloat *x, size_t limbs);
int bigFloatTruncate(BigFloat *x, size_t limbs);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Precision counts significant 32-bit limbs independently of storage capacity.
SetPrecision requires a positive size_t count, rounds toward zero if reducing
precision, normalizes the mantissa, and stores the policy on success.
Increasing precision preserves the stored value without restoring lost bits.
Truncate is an alias of SetPrecision and also changes the precision policy.
.PP
Normalize uses the current precision. A normalized nonzero mantissa has its
highest limb's bit 31 set; exp compensates for the shift. Zero is positive
with exponent zero. Final exponent range is checked before publishing.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 0, -1 for allocation failure, INT_MAX for an unrepresentable size or
exponent, or -2 for zero precision. Value and precision remain unchanged on
error. Truncate now returns status rather than setting errno.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bignums (3),
.BR bignums (7)
